cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Parking-Sharpness: a Lean 4 formalization of Sharpness and critical scaling of parking"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "Sharpness and
  critical scaling of parking" (Bou-Rabee and Panagiotis, arXiv:2609.02820): at
  the critical density the expected particle odometer of the parking process is
  comparable to the expected divisible sandpile odometer plus log n (Theorem
  1.2), hence of order n^((4-d)/4) for d <= 3 and log n for d >= 4 (Corollary
  1.3); below the critical density the settling time has a stretched-exponential
  tail with exponent d/(d+2) (Theorem 1.1); together with the quenched odometer
  comparison, the nearest hole and particle, near criticality and the oriented
  walk (Theorems 1.4 to 1.8) and every lemma and proposition behind them.
  Eighteen results the paper quotes from the literature are taken as explicit
  hypotheses.  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - parking
  - particle-hole process
  - divisible sandpile
  - random walk
